      "description": "HigherEdJobs | LinkedIn Agree & Join LinkedIn By clicking Continue to join or sign in, you agree to LinkedIn’s User Agreement , Privacy Policy , and Cookie Policy . Skip to main content LinkedIn Top Content People Learning Jobs Games Sign in Join now HigherEdJobs Higher Education State College, PA 223,921 followers Your higher ed job is here. Follow Discover all 260 employees Report this company About us HigherEdJobs® is the leading source for jobs and career information in academia. Last year, more than 289,950 faculty, administrative, and executive jobs were posted to the company’s website, which is visited by more than 1.6 million unique visitors each month. Serving the top universities and colleges throughout the nation and abroad, HigherEdJobs is the preeminent resource for connecting job seekers and higher education employers. Find your next job in higher education here! Website http://www.higheredjobs.com External link for HigherEdJobs Industry Higher Education Company size 11-50 employees Headquarters State College, PA Type Privately Held Founded 1996 Specialties higher education, recruitment, career advice, hiring resources, job search, faculty, administration, research, executive, colleges, and universities Employees at HigherEdJobs Alison Herget LinkedIn Member LinkedIn Member LinkedIn Member LinkedIn Member LinkedIn Member View 260 employees at HigherEdJobs Sign in Welcome back Email or phone Password Show Forgot password? Sign in or By clicking Continue to join or sign in, you agree to LinkedIn’s User Agreement , Privacy Policy , and Cookie Policy . New to LinkedIn? Join now or By clicking Continue to join or sign in, you agree to LinkedIn’s User Agreement , Privacy Policy , and Cookie Policy . See all employees Locations Primary 328 Innovation Blvd. Suite 235 State College, PA 16803, US Get directions 715 Lake Street Suite 400 Oak Park, IL 60301, US Get directions Updates HigherEdJobs 223,921 followers 22m Report this post AI can help students complete assignments faster. But does faster always mean better learning?\n\nEmerging research suggests that how students use AI matters — from critical thinking and knowledge retention to the ability to work through challenging concepts independently.\nFor faculty and higher education leaders, the question isn't simply whether to use AI. It's how to use it without losing what makes learning meaningful.\n\nWhat does the research actually say? Read the article to explore the findings 👉 https://lnkd.in/e2gDBM4K #HigherEducation #AIinEducation #TeachingAndLearning 1 Like Comment Share HigherEdJobs 223,921 followers 21h Report this post How to Build Trust: Consistency Takes Time | Full episode at https://lnkd.in/exQ-E3_r …more Play Video Video Player is loading. Loaded : 8.05% 0:00 Play Back to start Stream Type LIVE Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:31 1x Playback Rate Show Captions Mute Fullscreen Like Comment Share HigherEdJobs 223,921 followers 1d Report this post \"Best practices\" don't always yield best results - especially when working with student veterans. HigherEdMilitary shares a different perspective when choosing your approach. 👉Read more https://lnkd.in/ecTJZBxu Beyond ‘Best Practices’: Rethinking How We Build Cultures of Veteran Support in Higher Education Like Comment Share HigherEdJobs 223,921 followers 1d Report this post How to Earn Respect: Build Trust Without Taking It Personally | Full episode at https://lnkd.in/eExGj6-U …more Play Video Video Player is loading. Loaded : 24.97% 0:00 Play Back to start Stream Type LIVE Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:25 1x Playback Rate Show Captions Mute Fullscreen Like Comment Share HigherEdJobs 223,921 followers 2d Report this post Job seekers need to up their game and build more area-specific knowledge. Learn how career centers are supporting job seekers and how their strategies can help you. 👉Read more https://lnkd.in/eHv6yyu2 1 Like Comment Share HigherEdJobs 223,921 followers 2d Report this post Our Sales Account Manager Denee Anderson sat down with Gale Force Wins at the National Association of Career Colleges (NACC) #NACC2026 Conference to talk about her tenure at HigherEdJobs, what makes us stand apart from other job boards, and how HEJ continues to be the number one trusted source for higher ed talent after 30 years. \n\nWATCH the interview here: https://lnkd.in/e-SDPpgJ 8 Like Comment Share HigherEdJobs 223,921 followers 2d Report this post Why aren't you being given the full scope of your new role? It's not about you. Full episode: https://lnkd.in/eA2MMZ4x …more Play Video Video Player is loading. Loaded : 18.43% 0:00 Play Back to start Stream Type LIVE Current Time 0:00 / Duration 0:17 1x Playback Rate Show Captions Mute Fullscreen 1 Like Comment Share HigherEdJobs 223,921 followers 3d Report this post Two career professionals share how to prepare for the first step of the interview process: the phone interview. 👉Learn more https://lnkd.in/ecDkA-GT #careercoaching #interviewtips #jobssearchadvice 3 Like Comment Share HigherEdJobs 223,921 followers 3d Report this post Tune in as our guest - an author, leadership coach, and VP of student life - answers the question: What role does self-reflection play in navigating a career crossroads? 🎧Listen at https://lnkd.in/eFdu7S7R #podcast #careeradvice #selfreflection #careercoaching 1 Like Comment Share HigherEdJobs 223,921 followers 3d Report this post The rise of AI and the shifting political landscape are among the many changes that higher ed has navigated over the last 5 years. See which ones HR professionals say have made the biggest impact on their recruitment processes. #highered #recruitment #hiringtrends The Biggest Trends Shaping Higher Ed Recruitment HigherEdJobs on LinkedIn 11 Like Comment Share Join now to see what you are missing Find people you know at HigherEdJobs Browse recommended jobs for you View all updates, news, and articles Join now Affiliated pages The HigherEdJobs Podcast Higher Educati